# SmartHarvest Retro-fit Landing Page - AI Development Guidelines

## Project Context
High-converting landing page for agricultural equipment retro-fitting services.
**Tagline:** "Upgrade the Iron. Keep the Legacy."
**Goal:** Convert farmers to request free €2,000 equipment compatibility checks.

## Technology Stack & Requirements

### Core Stack
- **Runtime:** Node.js 24.x (required, use `nvm use 24`)
- **Framework:** Vue 3.5+ with Composition API (`<script setup>`)
- **Language:** TypeScript 5.9+ (strict mode enabled)
- **Build Tool:** Vite 7.x
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4 (new @import syntax)
- **UI Components:** PrimeVue 4.5+ with Tailwind theme
- **Icons:** Lucide Vue Next
- **Animations:** AOS (Animate On Scroll)

### Critical Version Requirements
- Node.js >=24.0.0 (enforced, do NOT suggest downgrading)
- Vue 3.5.28+
- Vite 7.3.1+
- Tailwind CSS 4.2.0+ (v4 with new import system)
- PrimeVue 4.5.4+ (with @primeuix/themes)

## Development Standards

### TypeScript
- **Strict Mode:** Always enabled, no exceptions
- **Type Safety:** All props, emits, functions must be explicitly typed
- **No `any`:** Use proper types or `unknown` with type guards
- **Interfaces:** Define in `src/types/index.ts` for shared types
- **Component Props:** Use `defineProps<{ ... }>()` with interface/type

Example:
```typescript
interface Props {
  title: string
  count?: number
}
const props = defineProps<Props>()
```

### Vue 3 Best Practices
- **Composition API:** Use `<script setup>` exclusively
- **Reactivity:** Prefer `ref()` for primitive values, `reactive()` for objects
- **Event Emits:** Always type with `defineEmits<{ ... }>()`
- **Computed:** Use `computed()` for derived state
- **Props Validation:** TypeScript interfaces, not runtime validators

### Styling Rules
- **Tailwind v4:** Use `@import "tailwindcss"` syntax (NOT @tailwind directives)
- **Brand Colors:** Use custom colors defined in tailwind.config.js
  - `forest-green` (#2D5A27) - Primary/Agriculture
  - `industrial-amber` (#F59E0B) - Accent/CTA
  - `tech-slate` (#1E293B) - Text/Modern
- **Utility-First:** Prefer Tailwind utilities over custom CSS
- **Custom Components:** Define in `@layer components` when needed
- **Responsive:** Mobile-first approach (sm:, md:, lg:, xl:)

### Component Architecture
- **Single Responsibility:** Each component does one thing well
- **Prop Types:** All props must have TypeScript interfaces
- **Emits:** Type all custom events
- **Composables:** Extract reusable logic to `src/composables/`
- **File Naming:** PascalCase for components (e.g., `HeroSection.vue`)

### Code Quality
- **No `console.log`:** Remove before committing (use proper debugging)
- **Error Handling:** Always handle async errors and edge cases
- **Accessibility:** Use semantic HTML, ARIA labels where needed
- **Performance:** Lazy load images, use `v-show` vs `v-if` appropriately
- **Comments:** Document complex logic, remove obvious comments

## Brand & Design System

### Color Palette
```javascript
colors: {
  'forest-green': '#2D5A27',    // Primary - Trust & Agriculture
  'industrial-amber': '#F59E0B', // Accent - Action & Machinery  
  'tech-slate': '#1E293B',       // Secondary - Modern Tech
}
```

### Typography
- **Body:** Inter (font-sans)
- **Headers:** Roboto Condensed (font-display)
- **Sizes:** Use Tailwind's type scale (text-xl, text-2xl, etc.)

### Spacing & Layout
- **Container:** Use `.section-container` utility class
- **Padding:** Consistent py-16 or py-20 for sections
- **Gaps:** grid-gap-6 or gap-8 for consistency
- **Rounded:** Use rounded-xl (1rem) or rounded-2xl (1.5rem)

### Buttons
- **Primary:** `.btn-primary` (industrial-amber background)
- **Secondary:** `.btn-secondary` (forest-green background)
- **States:** Include hover, focus, disabled, loading

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── components/           # All Vue components
│   ├── NavigationHeader.vue
│   ├── HeroSection.vue
│   ├── PostcardBridge.vue
│   ├── ComparisonSection.vue
│   ├── BentoGrid.vue
│   ├── ProcessSection.vue
│   ├── ValueProposition.vue
│   ├── ClaimCheckModal.vue
│   └── FooterSection.vue
├── types/               # TypeScript type definitions
│   └── index.ts
├── composables/         # Reusable composition functions
├── App.vue             # Root component
├── main.ts             # App entry point
├── style.css           # Global styles + Tailwind
└── vite-env.d.ts       # Type declarations
```

## Component Guidelines

### Props Pattern
```typescript
interface Props {
  title: string
  optional?: number
}
const props = defineProps<Props>()
```

### Emits Pattern
```typescript
const emit = defineEmits<{
  (e: 'update', value: string): void
  (e: 'submit', data: FormData): void
}>()
```

### Reactive State
```typescript
import { ref, computed } from 'vue'

const count = ref(0)
const doubled = computed(() => count.value * 2)
```

## Animation Standards
- **AOS Attributes:** `data-aos="fade-up"`, `data-aos-delay="100"`
- **Timing:** 800ms duration, ease-in-out easing
- **Triggers:** Once on scroll (once: true)
- **Delays:** Stagger by 100-150ms for sequential items

## Form Handling
- **Validation:** Client-side with TypeScript types
- **Loading States:** Show loading indicator on submit
- **Success/Error:** Display appropriate feedback
- **Accessibility:** Proper labels, error messages, focus management

## Performance Requirements
- **Bundle Size:** Keep under 500KB (gzipped)
- **Images:** Use WebP format, lazy loading
- **Code Splitting:** Lazy load routes if adding more pages
- **Tree Shaking:** Import only what you use from libraries

## Testing Checklist
- [ ] TypeScript compiles without errors (`npm run build`)
- [ ] All interactive elements work on mobile
- [ ] Forms validate correctly
- [ ] Animations perform smoothly
- [ ] Responsive at all breakpoints (375px - 1920px)
- [ ] Accessibility: keyboard navigation, screen readers
- [ ] Browser testing: Chrome, Safari, Firefox, Edge

## Build & Deployment
- **Dev:** `npm run dev` (port 5173)
- **Build:** `npm run build` (outputs to `dist/`)
- **Preview:** `npm run preview` (test production build)
- **Node Version:** Always use Node 24 (`nvm use 24`)

## Common Issues & Solutions

### Issue: Tailwind classes not working
- **Solution:** Ensure Tailwind v4 import syntax in style.css
- Check: `@import "tailwindcss"` (NOT `@tailwind base`)

### Issue: PrimeVue components not styled
- **Solution:** Import `@primeuix/themes` and configure in main.ts

### Issue: TypeScript errors on build
- **Solution:** Check `tsconfig.json` baseUrl deprecation warnings
- Ensure all imports use `@/` alias or relative paths correctly

### Issue: AOS animations not triggering
- **Solution:** Verify AOS.init() called in main.ts after mount
- Check: `data-aos` attributes on elements

